 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 511119,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the intercepts of <span data-math=\"3x + y = 12\">3x + y = 12</span> and use them to graph the equation.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"3x + y = 12\"></span></p>\n<p>Let <i>y</i> = 0 to find the <i>x</i>-intercept.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"3x + 0 = 12\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"3x = 12\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"x = 4\"></span></p>\n<p><i>x-</i>intercept: (4, 0).</p>\n<p>Let <i>x</i> = 0 to find the <i>y</i>-intercept.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"3\\left( 0 \\right) + y = 12\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y = 12\"></span></p>\n<p><i>y-</i>intercept: (0, 12).</p>\n<p>Plot the intercepts and connect to graph the line.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The <span data-math=\"x\">x</span>-intercept is (4, 0) and the <span data-math=\"y\">y</span>-intercept is (0, 12).<br>\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBcUlQIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--a8f89db8d9a619ef877ec04ae4f420b7952e1900/CS_Figure_05_08_008.png\" alt=\"A line is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The x and y axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 1. The line passes through the following points, (0, 12), (4, 0), and (5, negative 3).\">"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
